The fuzz-test harness in this directory is adapted from Strata
Contributors' work at https://github.com/strata-org/Strata, specifically
the files

  Tools/Python/scripts/hypothesmith.sh
  Tools/Python/scripts/gen_random_python.py
  Tools/Python/scripts/gen_unrestricted.py
  .github/workflows/python-fuzz.yml

on the origin/tautschnig/hypothesmith branch.

These upstream files are licensed under Apache-2.0 OR MIT (Strata's dual
license). The CBMC-side adaptation:

  - python-fuzz.sh        (driver, was hypothesmith.sh)
  - .github/workflows/python-fuzz.yaml (was python-fuzz.yml)

retargets the harness from Strata's pyAnalyzeLaurel pipeline to CBMC's
Python frontend. The program-generator scripts (gen_random_python.py,
gen_unrestricted.py) are functionally unchanged from upstream; the
modifications are limited to copyright headers, module docstrings, and
references to the consuming tool.

The hypothesmith library that drives syntax-mode generation is a
third-party dependency installed at runtime into a Python virtual
environment; see https://github.com/Zac-HD/hypothesmith and its own
license for redistribution terms.
